WEBVTT

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.910
Rikukaikuu doko ni ikou
Where to go? The land, sea or sky?

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.370
Ahiru no Sora

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.000
Kimi o sasoitai na
I wanna invite you to come along

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:25.830
Monogatari wa hajima tterunda
The pages of our story have started to turn

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.550
Okubyou kaze mo recycle
If you lose your nerve then recycle it

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.550
Mayotteru senaka oshite
And let it push you past hesitation

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.760
Give and go! Isogou
Give and go! With the flow

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:47.860
Mogutteita honou ga kaodashite
Instincts that are buried deep will always rear their head again

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:55.070
Kakusenai no sa yume ni mita yume
People can't just hide the dreams they once dreamed of

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.490
Tobenai tsubasa demo
Even if these wings can't fly

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:05.370
Bokura wa habataite sora o kanjitai
We want to spread them wide and embrace the sky

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.710
Naritai jibun ni naritai
Becoming the people who we want to be

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:15.380
Ima dekinai koto mo ashita wa wakannai ze
You never know, the impossible could be possible tomorrow

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.840
Waru agaki shiyou
So let's keep up the struggle

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.890
Happy go ducky!

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.540
The 2-3 zone.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.710
It's the most commonly used formation
when playing zone defense.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.710
My dear Nao...

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.250
I know that zone defense is full of your love,
so I'll fill our offense with my own.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.960
Quit wasting time! Just get on with it!

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.590
Get your guard up, girls!

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:53.960
Here they come!

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.130
Sweet.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.170
Got it?

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.750
Whenever you receive a pass,
you have to take stock of the situation around you.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.000
Look for anybody who is open.
And check for empty space in front of you.  

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.210
Okay! I'll handle this!

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.840
Hey, Yasu! Over here!

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.710
Nice, Chucky!

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.590
I've got him!

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:18.340
Sayuri!

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.880
Shit... I still can't dribble the ball properly...

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.630
A screen!

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.000
Yoko, in the middle!

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.210
Over here!

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.000
Oh, Nabe is free!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.420
Time is up! 24-second violation!

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.920
I totally forgot.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.380
We only have 24 seconds to take a shot
when we're on offense, right?

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.340
Sorry, it's all because I was lagging behind.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.130
Nah, you're doing fine as-is.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.880
Don't try and rush it, just stay aware
of your surroundings.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:00.540
The role of each player in a zone defense
is much more ambiguous than in man-to-man.  

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.790
So sometimes it's possible for them
to end up overlapping like you just saw.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.380
And if two defenders end up
covering the same player, then what happens?

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.710
I get it, that means somebody else is left open.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.670
Their current zone defense
was hastily prepared to counter us.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.790
Holes are bound to open up in it eventually.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.590
Momoharu and I will focus on making those holes.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.590
Make sure you watch closely.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.230
Boys

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.230
Girls

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.210
Nice three-pointer, Yoko!

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.880
I just remembered something Kite said to us.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.340
Whenever we get the ball, we should always look at...

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:41.750
...the basket!

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.250
What the hell is she doing?

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.040
H-he isn't going to take a shot...?

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.960
And now I blow past her. Is that how this works?

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:54.000
That was smooth! When did Yasu actually get that good?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.460
Gah! Oh shi-!

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.340
Whoa there!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.040
Nice one, Nabe!

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:05.420
What the hell are you passing
to the other team for, dumbass?!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.180
Kurumatani: 3-Pointers, speed

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.180
Chucky: Calm and can analyze...

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.180
Nabe: Awarenes is...

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.180
Yasuhara: Ball handling needs...

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.380
Like you're one to talk, what kind of dribbling was that?!

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.000
When Yasu went for that drive just now,
it opened another hole in the defense.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.040
Did you see it?

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:16.590
Yeah. I saw it.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.040
Dummy! What were you thinking?!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.750
The defender that was in front of me
took off to try and block Yasu.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.340
It left me totally free on the opposite side.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:28.090
The zone defense makes it relatively easy
for members of the offense to get open.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.090
By repeating a cycle of passes and drives,
it will eventually fall apart.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.430
Boys

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.430
Girls

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:50.590
It was a mistake to let him handle anything.
The other team is just widening the gap on us.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.340
I'm starting to think that Bro had no idea
what he was doing this whole time.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.290
The only players without an idea
of what they're doing are you two.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:04.210
The reason I said this team would never win,
is because you lack something very fundamental.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.920
"Something fundamental"?

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:06.670
Yep.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.880
What every team needs
to deal with screens and zone defense,

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.210
is absolute faith in each other's ability to provide cover.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:19.210
Having players who think they can just use other skills
to cover their own weaknesses

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.840
prevents the team from functioning as a whole.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:29.670
The one thing this team needs in order to win,
is for every player to embrace their own shortcomings.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
Chiaki:

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
wide field of vision, passes

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
 Everyone must embrace shortcomings

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
Must work on individual scoring

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
and making the best of situations

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
must learn how to coordinate

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
(screens and pass work)

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
(Overall) Lacking stamina

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.390
Refine fundamentals, especially footwork

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.250
And then use teamwork to adequately make up for those.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.920
You know what they say: There is no "I" in "TEAM."

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.040
That's a fundamental part of basketball.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.340
Okay! Do it now!

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.750
Somebody get on him!

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.880
Incredible! He's totally free right in front of the basket!

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.420
A-amazing...

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.460
See that? Hope you're watching, little birdies!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.920
I am a genius on the court!

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.770
Boys

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.770
Girls

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.210
Game over!

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:21.540
The girls' win with 18 points to 5!

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.500
All right!

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.630
Thank God! My body has been saved from ogling eyes!

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.130
Whoops! I totally spaced
that Momoharu can't shoot to save his life.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:37.710
Note: Lyrics from the 1974 enka song, "Showa Kare Susuki."

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:37.960
We lost to poverty~!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:43.290
Hold up! We didn't lose to poverty or anything like that!
We lost to the girls' team!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.880
Just forget about the inter-high or whatever.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.920
I don't think we could even
beat a team of kids from elementary school.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.880
I've lost every last ounce of motivation, man.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.130
Uh, wait! Come on, you guys.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.460
Yasuhara!

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:00.090
Nabe?!

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:02.380
Chucky!

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.840
N-not good...

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.880
Momoharu, please say something to bring them around!

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:13.630
Oh, jeez! All we have to do is get better
by practicing more!

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.130
Right, Nanao?

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.340
Huh?

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.840
Wh-where did she go?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.380
I screwed it up again.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.920
I really only meant for it to be a little test of their skill.

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:31.460
Making them lose motivation is the exact opposite
of what a manager is supposed to do, ugh...

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:34.540
I can't figure it out. Why am I so bad at this?

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.710
It's like I have no ability to learn fro-

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.040
How lame!

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.750
She's like a manga character!
I've never seen anybody fall in the gutter for real!

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:45.460
Same!

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:46.500
Nanao!

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.710
Kurumatani...?

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.540
You left so fast, I thought something might be wrong.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.790
Here, you forgot this.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:54.960
Thanks...

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.840
Wh-what happened to... your leg?

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:06.210
P-please accept my apologies.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.460
It's no big deal.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.790
My grandma makes me take care
of the cleaning all the time.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.130
Not that.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.000
That's not what I'm apologizing for.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:19.420
In that match earlier, my strategy
totally singled you out on every play...

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.460
Uh, that's okay, no need to apologize to me.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:27.340
I know that's just what it takes to win the game, right?

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.000
Well, I'm a bit on the obsessive side.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.210
I always throw everything I have into it,
without even thinking.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.540
Back in middle school,
stuff like this happened to me so much.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.410
GIRLS'

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.410
BASKETBALL

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.410
DISTRICT TOURNAMENT

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.590
Like back before the semi-finals
of our district tournament...

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.340
Our frontcourt game is weak!
We need to shore ourselves up in the middle!

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:51.460
Kosugi

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.170
Should we leave the defense as-is?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.840
Yeah. We don't want to ruin our rhythm
by changing anything we don't have to.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.040
U-um, I think that we should sub out numbers 4 and 5.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.540
Huh?

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:00.920
There's not much time left,
so we should focus our defense in the paint.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:04.040
That's why we should put in taller players
like Matsuki and Taniguchi.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.880
Don't be stupid! I'm the team captain
and Miyuki is the vice-captain!

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:11.130
Why should we ever sub out for two younger players?

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.130
B-but that's what we need to win...

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:17.170
A manager like you has no right
to be making important calls like that!

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.420
Just keep your nose out of this and your own business!

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.630
It should have been obvious to me...

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:28.630
I was out of line telling the seniors to sub out
for freshmen at such a crucial moment.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:33.420
There are a lot of other important things to consider
than just winning and losing.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.920
For sure...

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:40.630
Honestly, I think I'm better off just as a spectator
than being a part of the team.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.090
My motive for wanting to join
was kind of immodest, anyway.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:44.790
Huh?

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.960
Keep doing your best out there.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:50.090
I think your team... will be a force to be reckoned with.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.960
Nanao...

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.380
Ouch!

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:57.790
Is she really gonna be okay?

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:01.590
She forgot it again?!

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:17.750
I think... she meant that she was going to quit the team.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.960
No... say it ain't so!

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.590
Tell me, how am I supposed to keep on living now?

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.040
Who cares?

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.960
Let her quit if she wants.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.960
We don't need a manager who wastes time
pretending to be a coach.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.040
You don't have to be so rude about it.  

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.380
Nanao was just trying her best to help us all!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:41.460
To make a good coach,
you pretty much have to be a former player.  

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:44.880
It's years of experience
that give a coach sufficient insight.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:49.750
I'm not going to let a brat with no first-hand
experience tell me how to play the game.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.340
That's not fair, she told us she was
on a basketball team back in middle school!

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.250
Yeah, but she was still just a manager.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:01.210
The only thing a manager should do is take care
of the odd jobs that nobody else has time for.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.670
Why do you always have to be such an asshole?!

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:06.000
Have some decency!

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.920
What? You wanna take this outside, shrimp?

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:15.290
What's all this?

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.840
They're notes from our game...

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:21.960
Whoa, this is nuts! There's more than 20 pages of stuff!

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:27.210
"Yasuhara has a good sense for driving,
but must work on improving his handling of the ball."

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.210
Hey! Is there anything about me in there?

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.960
Dude, I'm looking at what she wrote about me.
Just wait a damn minute!

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:34.340
That takes me back. She was always doing stuff like that.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:39.000
I can tell you about Nao.
There's one part of her story that you don't know yet.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:43.500
The truth is, she's been playing basketball
ever since she was a kid.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:44.880
Huh?

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.880
She switched to being a manager
in the summer of her 2nd year at middle school.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.840
Up until then, she practiced with us
as a member of the team.

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:54.500
She switched? Because of an injury or what?

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.710
Nope. She was in perfect shape.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.130
I don't recall her ever suffering an injury.

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:00.420
But then, why the change?

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:05.040
She just wasn't suited to... the game of basketball.

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:07.630
Just think about it.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:11.420
Sora is a good example of someone
who doesn't have the stature necessary for basketball,

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:15.170
but his speedy footwork and great shooting sense
make up for that disadvantage.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:20.040
Naturally, we know that's the result of him
going through a lot of blood, sweat, and tears.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:25.790
But some people in the world can never make up
the difference, no matter how hard they try.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:30.340
Nao was one of them and that's why
she desperately tried to find her own path,

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:33.040
and eventually armed herself
with the weapon we call "strategy."

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.210
She read a ton of basketball books,

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.710
watched an endless amount of games,

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:42.250
and constantly scouted out
our opponents from other schools.

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:45.670
Unfortunately, her suggestions did lead
to some fights among the team,

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.710
but her analysis of the situation was never wrong.

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:53.340
She didn't become the manager of your team
just to do a bunch of odd jobs.   

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:57.710
She wants to be involved in the sport she loves,
in any way that she can.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.170
Is that really such a terrible thing?

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:09.250
Awesome! That means she has incredible talent!

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:13.250
Nanao accomplished exactly what Kite was talking about
by dedicating herself

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:18.630
to mastering all of the knowledge that
a top-notch coach would have after years of play!

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:22.340
You guys should hurry and chase after her.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.340
She's going to be your manager, right?

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.500
R-right.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.420
Senpai...

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.630
Please let me use the showers
in the girl's changing room!

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:32.420
What the heck happened to you?!

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:37.540
I was catching crayfish with some kids
when I fell into the water...

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.090
Yo. Thanks for this.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:43.960
Wait, how did you...?

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.000
You forgot it back at the park.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.790
Seriously, this is downright incredible.

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:55.170
You didn't just lay out all of our failings,
you also made detailed notes on how we can fix them.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:59.540
If we practice all that stuff you wrote down,
will we get better?

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.130
If there's anything else we can do, let us know, yeah?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:06.460
My dear Nao, you don't have to do a thing for me.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.630
Just having you here is enough to-

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:09.750
Why are you the only one going full creeper?!

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:14.840
I hope you'll do more than just be our manager.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.750
Let's play together sometime!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.380
I know you can play basketball,
so it would be a waste not to!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.380
Are you sure?

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.290
Can I really be your manager?

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.380
Of course!

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:37.380
Real talk though, our advisor is a total noob.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.380
You'd be saving our asses
if you could act as our coach, too.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.960
I'm a pretty strict coach, you know.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:45.000
Great. That's exactly what we need.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:46.960
Hey, little lady.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:52.210
Don't you dare think that you got the better of me
with that weakass zone defense of yours.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:54.670
Just watch this.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.170
A 3-pointer...?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:02.210
Seriously? He can shoot from long-range, too?

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.750
I was subbed out before I had the chance
to bring my A-game.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.920
I never lost to you or your strategy, got it?

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:13.750
In that case, I would have tweaked our zone
and shut you down with the triangle and 2 defense!

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:18.670
This damn half-pint...!

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.130
This cocky pineapple head...!

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.710
Uh, let's get along please! No fighting!

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.040
Go!

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.880
Hey, Nabe! You need to react faster!

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:37.540
Okay!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.840
Round 12!

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:41.540
You're not allowed to turn around until you hear me clap!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.630
Keep your hands up in the air
until you hear me give the sign!

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:48.340
No lying down during the intervals!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.090
Please keep your breathing steady with a light jog!

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.130
She's a demon...

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:54.040
A dictator...

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.130
Since the volleyball team has the gym
today we had no other choice,

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:01.460
but doing this practice out on the court
would be so much more effective...

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.880
A training camp?

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:05.960
Yes.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:08.540
This weekend is the start of the Golden Week holiday,

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:11.130
so there's only one month left
until the inter-high prelims begin.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:13.670
We absolutely cannot afford
to let this opportunity pass us by.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:17.380
Are we seriously going to practice
through the entire holiday?

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:21.920
So like, is the inter-high just impossible for us
without doing all this work?

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:25.000
In order for Kuzu High to actually reach the inter-high,

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:29.540
we must win the prelims and become
a representative team for the Kanagawa region.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.340
Knockout League

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.340
Win

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.340
Lose

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.340
Score

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.340
Rank

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:32.460
The knockout league that decides
the representative teams

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.840
consists of 4 schools that survive the prefectural prelims.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:39.670
And to even enter the prefectural prelims,
we first have claim victory in the district tournament.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:44.210
Out of hundreds of schools, there are only 2
who can become representatives for the inter-high.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:49.790
The number of victories required to become
a representative team is 10, at the very least.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:55.170
I believe that it would be difficult for our team
to even win a single game as we are now.

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:57.750
It just never ends...

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:02.170
Now, now, now... There's always
a bright side to find, gentlemen.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:04.250
It's Golden Week...

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:08.750
Places like the Nasu Highlands or Karuizawa are
probably booked full with students from university clubs.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.290
And at this time, the beaches of Okinawa
should be open for swimming.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.920
Just imagine what it would be like
to have our training camp in a place like that.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.920
Oh... Okiniawa...

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:36.290
YES! YES! YES!

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.880
A training camp, huh?

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:39.000
That's a solid idea for us to start refining our teamwork.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:41.420
We swear to survive whatever harsh training they can throw at us!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:42.210
Each of us will need to level up our individual skills, too.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:44.210
Awesome...

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:47.000
Being able to spend a whole day on basketball
is like a dream!

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:53.250
That sums it up, Mr. Satsuki. Can you reserve a location
for the camp and work the expenses into our budget?

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:54.630
Okinawa Okinawa! Okinawa!

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:54.630
Budget?

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.090
There's no budget for this team.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:59.710
No... No way!

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:03.540
The basketball team was nothing
but a hangout for hoodlums until recently.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:06.000
The school would never provide
any money considering that.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.670
No budget... not even a single yen?

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:12.380
If we file a formal application,
then there might be a chance.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:14.460
But I expect it would just be a drop in the bucket.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:16.630
Okay then, boys...

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.170
...we have no choice but to fall back on our last resort!

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.660
SAFETY

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.660
FIRST

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.420
Work for the money!

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.540
These are way too heavy!

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.900
Kanagawa School of Medical Science

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.900
Secondary Hospital

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.960
I don't wanna drink it!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:09.960
The reason you aren't getting any taller
is because you're always so picky like that, Sora.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:14.340
But it's so white and yucky! And yucky and white!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:15.920
Oh really?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.000
Well I happen to love it.

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:20.630
I've been drinking it ever since I was a little kid.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:23.790
That makes you living proof that this stuff doesn't work.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.460
I'll never get any taller by drinking it!

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.880
That's it, Sora. No dinner for you tonight!

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:32.500
What?! That's abuse! Tyranny!

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:35.290
I'm gonna call child protective services!

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:43.420
What's wrong? Did your bike get a flat tire?

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:46.340
Oh crap! It's already past 6!

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.840
And I've still got half of them left to deliver!

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:54.040
Say, Miss, are you a nurse here?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.710
Yes, I am.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.420
I-in the third ward...

00:19:58.420 --> 00:19:59.290
Huh?

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:02.130
No, nevermind. Just forget it.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.540
Here. Please drink this!

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.300
Thunder Brand

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.300
Milk

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.670
Thanks for your hard work!

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.670
See ya!

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:09.250
Huh? Um, hey, wait kid!

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:10.290
Gotta hurry!

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.780
YUKA KURUMATANI

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.790
Hm? Is this milk?

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.250
Oh, yeah.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:28.670
I don't know why, but a small delivery boy
gave it to me. As a gift.

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:32.500
It seemed like maybe someone he knew
was hospitalized here.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.420
From: Sora

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.420
G'morning.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.630
Excuse me, Ms. Yabuuchi?

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.290
Yes?

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:43.090
If it's all right with you, could I have this?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.290
I love a nice glass of milk!

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.920
Forget about Okinawa,
this amount wouldn't even get us to Shonan.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:59.090
Well, that's about the best we could hope for
from only a day's worth of work.

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:00.130
Hold up.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.670
Don't go forgetting about us now.

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:07.670
Just wait and see. We'll bring back over 10 times
your investment in an hour, tops!

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.500
Sorry!

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:12.670
You goddamn idiots!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.630
Did you guys forget that you're still in high school?!

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:21.130
Just be patient and let Mr. Satsuki and I
handle our funding issues!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:26.500
For the time being, Mr. Satsuki was kind enough
to provide us with some money from his own pocket!

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:29.290
Okay, fam!

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:32.590
The beautiful shores of Okinawa are waiting for us!

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:34.210
YES!

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:36.710
Yeah... about that.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:40.630
Our training camp will be held entirely here at school.

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:44.840
By the way, in order to cut costs as much as possible,

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Training Camp Requirements

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Cost - 3,000 yen per person

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Rice - 3kg per person

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Fresh veggies, fish, etc

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
(everyone brings what they can)

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Futons - BYO

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Fresh clothes - pair for every day

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:47.780
Snacks - up to 300-yen worth

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.840
we will be responsible for preparing everything
that we feasibly can!

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:51.710
This is starting to sound more
like a survival camp than a training camp.

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:55.130
Excuse me... I'd like to withdraw from participating.

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:56.090
Request denied!

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.670
We're all in this together, so let's do our best!

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:18.600
Doredake sora o miagetatte
It didn't matter how long you stared up at the sky

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:21.860
Boku wa tobenai to kimi wa itta
You always said that you would never be able to fly

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:25.070
Ato nankai te o nobaseba
One night I cried wondering how long it would take

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:28.450
Todoku no darou to naita yoru
Until I could finally reach you with my hands

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:31.950
Nigedasu koto ni nareteitte
Eventually I got used to just running away

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:35.250
Sore ga yowasa dato shitta ano hi
Until the day I realized that was a weakness

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:39.460
Hajimeyou mata, kyou kara
So let's start it all over, right now

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:48.090
Taisetsu na mono wa itsudemo soba ni atta
The things precious to us were always close at hand

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:54.430
Bokura wa itsumo hitori janai donna toki mo
We are never completely alone at any time in our lives

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:57.730
Toberu sa doko made mo kimi wa
The truth is that you can fly, wherever you want

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:01.480
Dare yori tataku tataku habataite
Spreading your wings to go far higher than anyone else

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:05.740
Nagashita namida no kazu dake
The more tears that you shed

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:07.700
Tsuyoku narunda
Then the stronger you become

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:11.070
Tsubasa hiroge sekai o megutte
Let's use those wings to travel the world over

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:14.660
Dare mo shiranai mirai o sagasou
And find a path to a future that no one knows about

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:19.250
Zutto, zutto, zutto
Always, always, always

00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:22.920
Aruite yukou saa, issho ni
Walking onwards, all of us together

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:35.390
Ahiru no Sora

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:35.390
Next Time: Differing Enthusiasm

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:34.590
Next time: "Differing Enthusiasm."
